#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pantheon-club: a club view of a Pantheon network, as the first tab of its cmux workspace.

The actual Claude Penguin game runs locally. Market participants appear as
native penguins and cloud workers as matching puffles in your own igloo.
Your player can travel around the original game; agents stay in the igloo.
Run scripts/setup-game once first (Node 24+, Python 3.10+, Git, npm).

  pantheon-club game NET|RECORD|demo [--port N]
                        full upstream game, local only (default port 8767);
                        Ctrl-C stops all three local services

  pantheon-club up NET [PANTHEON-CMUX UP ARGS...]
                        pantheon-cmux up NET with these arguments, then attach
  pantheon-club attach NET
                        the club tab, first in the left half of NET's workspace
                        (before the plan and the watchdog), and its server
  pantheon-club down NET
                        stop the club's server, then pantheon-cmux down NET
  pantheon-club serve NET [--port N]
                        alias for game, using the full local game
  pantheon-club state NET|RECORD
                        the state the view draws, as JSON
  pantheon-club view RECORD|demo [--port N]
                        alias for game; no cmux needed for demo or records
  pantheon-club legacy-view RECORD|demo [--port N]
                        preserved Coffee Shop prototype for comparison only
  pantheon-club worker NET NAME --parent DIPLOMAT [--state STATE] [--task TEXT]
                        register or update a spawned provider cloud task as a
                        puffle; --remove dismisses it. attach also installs a
                        club-worker helper in each diplomat's desk.

A node without a diplomat came from the diplomat named in NET/NODE/parent, when
that file is there (whoever starts the node can write it); else from the
diplomat whose name starts its name (claude-cloud1 from claude); else from a
diplomat of its provider (claude-b from claude-a); else from none.

Settings, from the environment:
  PANTHEON_CMUX  pantheon-cmux (default: on PATH, else ../pantheon/integrations/cmux/pantheon-cmux
                 beside this checkout, else beside $PANTHEON)
  CMUX           the cmux CLI (default: cmux on PATH, else the one inside cmux.app)

Attached game metadata, logs, player database and tab id live in NET/.cmux/club.
Standalone player data lives in this checkout's .local-game directory.
"""

